      "id": 1,
      "text": "Daviston may be named after the Davis family, who were among the early settlers in the late 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/daviston_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early pioneers in Daviston cleared land along the Great Pee Dee and Catfish Creek to establish rural farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/daviston_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The early economy of Daviston centered on small-scale farming and timber extraction within the Pee Dee region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/daviston_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Daviston's agricultural history shifted from cotton to tobacco in the 1920s after boll weevil infestations ravaged local fields.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/daviston_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Old Neck Cemetery served as a focal point for local families during the community's emergence in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/daviston_south_carolina"
    },
    {
